<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:45:00Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Harvey Weinstein resentenced to 15 years for sexual assault</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af71bcf750b46b5c8c6e295e932fe196af22f8f1ad904b475a9267847ea5931b</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:44:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T17:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/harvey-weinstein-resentenced-to-15-years-for-sexual-assault/a-79403381--8507b6a2aba6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/harvey-weinstein-resentenced-to-15-years-for-sexual-assault/a-79403381?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The disgraced Hollywood mogul was found guilty of sexually assaulting former production assistant Miriam Haley. The man whose case spurred the #MeToo movement awaits a separate sentencing in a California rape case.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>New fighting in Ethiopia's Tigray region raises fears of a return to the country's civil war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1a7c6a516487ad79600b46fde36f2ecc664b19df8c640643bc465369ff3d2d43</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:44:42Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T17:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-fighting-in-ethiopia-s-tigray-region-raises-fears-of-a-return-to-the-country-s-civil-war/a-79400869--cb917e424fac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-fighting-in-ethiopia-s-tigray-region-raises-fears-of-a-return-to-the-country-s-civil-war/a-79400869?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fighting in and around Tigray is testing Ethiopia's fragile 2022 peace deal. With old enemies forming new alliances, experts warn that the conflict could enter a dangerous new phase.</summary><category term="NRS-Import" /></entry><entry><title>Eviction of 87-year-old woman sparks housing protests in Madrid</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1e6d5ed47cfc9d24157fc4785f80b47574e58801a3aa3da2f442163420d8be2</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:44:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T16:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eviction-of-87-year-old-woman-sparks-housing-protests-in-madrid/a-79399342--1588b5df3843.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eviction-of-87-year-old-woman-sparks-housing-protests-in-madrid/a-79399342?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police escorted Maricarmen Abascal from the apartment she had called home for more than seven decades. The case has reignited debate over Spain's housing crisis, rising rents and protections for long-term tenants.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump's Board of Peace proposes $2.45B for reconstruction in Gaza</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e3c65842efdad6f27c7babe57ab07f5e7baf04c96bc10a1982232b344fde415a</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:44:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T16:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-s-board-of-peace-proposes-2-45b-for-reconstruction-in-gaza/a-79401612--59213d247592.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-s-board-of-peace-proposes-2-45b-for-reconstruction-in-gaza/a-79401612?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The board has noted that the Palestinian enclave needs roughly $35.2 billion for full, medium-term reconstruction. Trump's plan for peace in Gaza has largely stalled since an agreement was reached almost a year ago.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Who is skipping the UN General Assembly — and why</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8647b2966b00d4d2171e10e15f60ee78ae70795bc90f2f13de40404e14546075</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:44:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-is-skipping-the-un-general-assembly-and-why/a-79391652--2b8efddbdd7a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-is-skipping-the-un-general-assembly-and-why/a-79391652?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Xi Jinping, Vladimir Putin, Friedrich Merz, Giorgia Meloni and Mahmoud Abbas are among more than 50 leaders who won't make it to the UN General Assembly. Their reasons range from illness and domestic affairs to holidays.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Could a Left Party government in Berlin expropriate large real estate companies?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed3c820c192932153e696269e08f6890ddb59b44c98f1ad8606052ecd17c47eb</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:44:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T14:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-a-left-party-government-in-berlin-expropriate-large-real-estate-companies/a-79399683--c9f46d7db0c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-a-left-party-government-in-berlin-expropriate-large-real-estate-companies/a-79399683?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The socialist Left Party won the Berlin election partly on the promise to implement the city's 2021 expropriation referendum as a way to solve the city's rent crisis. But can it really happen?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>China's 13-year-old swimming star raises questions on child athletes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a303ccbbeb10e0baff99febb5e8b2f3d2d6086f90ba0cc1a7396981fc39aaeb9</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:44:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T14:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-13-year-old-swimming-star-raises-questions-on-child-athletes/a-79394183--95db71a677f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-13-year-old-swimming-star-raises-questions-on-child-athletes/a-79394183?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Three gold medals and three Asian Games records have catapulted China's Yu Zidi, 13, into the sporting spotlight. She is far from the first teen prodigy, but should teens be competing at elite level?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan's jailed former PM Khan's sons told DW the authorities are cracking down ahead of new PTI protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79252b87238ff9129cef088afbaaadf00df9b59c23236315cfb8d0800e351e79</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:43:41Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-s-jailed-former-pm-khan-s-sons-told-dw-the-authorities-are-cracking-down-ahead-of-new-pti-p/a-79392147--8ea0d4621d28.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-s-jailed-former-pm-khan-s-sons-told-dw-the-authorities-are-cracking-down-ahead-of-new-pti-protests/a-79392147?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The sons of jailed Pakistani ex-PM Imran Khan told DW their father is in ill health while being isolated from family and doctors. Other relatives have been detained ahead of a planned opposition protest.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Slovakia: PM Robert Fico's NATO Article 5 remarks spark criticism and raise questions about his country's NATO commitment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:480b5029c7b5a109c8aba30e26e51bbbec8d0de45e204a2b02aaac626c9df87e</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:43:41Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/slovakia-pm-robert-fico-s-nato-article-5-remarks-spark-criticism-and-raise-questions-about-his-count/a-79387050--e3e0d18cd9d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/slovakia-pm-robert-fico-s-nato-article-5-remarks-spark-criticism-and-raise-questions-about-his-country-s-nato-commitment/a-79387050?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Slovak Prime Minister Robert Fico says he fears war and will do everything he can to keep his country out of one. Critics say his remarks risk weakening NATO, the alliance that was designed to prevent such a war.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's oldest party, the center-left SPD, is in a difficult position following its success in the Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania state election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77062f94761105e51a42e3d13ed2e7bd2b968d10b7a94ea048bc6b34041a2880</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:43:41Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-oldest-party-the-center-left-spd-is-in-a-difficult-position-following-its-success-in-the-m/a-79376827--2a4f42a68594.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-oldest-party-the-center-left-spd-is-in-a-difficult-position-following-its-success-in-the-mecklenburg-western-pomerania-state-election/a-79376827?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz (CDU) has vowed to press ahead with controversial reforms, but resistance is mounting within his coalition partner, the SPD. How much dissent can a governing coalition tolerate?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia: Fighting resumes in Tigray</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b7beaa94fc47664ab849e37b8720d344f9ec5483ce66397713ffc12892eec3b</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:43:41Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T12:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-fighting-resumes-in-tigray/a-79394192--9abf0a9cd5c1.html" type="text/html" /><l