loc-to-bloc agreement between the EU and ASEAN remains a distant prospect.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Munich, Berlin, Cologne-Rhine-Ruhr – Germany's three Olympic candidates</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2b5c42cfee653559a88fd620a22f763331f97b9586bee9f8a2e8f56a04abf77</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:43:41Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T11:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/munich-berlin-cologne-rhine-ruhr-germany-s-three-olympic-candidates/a-79386915--56e9e5ef3aab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/munich-berlin-cologne-rhine-ruhr-germany-s-three-olympic-candidates/a-79386915?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Munich, Berlin, or the Cologne-Rhine-Ruhr region? Germany aims to host the Olympic Games again. Three candidates are in the running, with one city considered the slight favorite.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Rome's Colosseum closes after worker falls to his death</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5dc73cb00821fba756bb442f227a078f773f62b0cb960bc6eb3b55dcda8861ff</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:43:41Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T10:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rome-s-colosseum-closes-after-worker-falls-to-his-death/a-79387180--030a6ce0cdab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rome-s-colosseum-closes-after-worker-falls-to-his-death/a-79387180?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The man had been working on a new lighting installation in the iconic Roman amphitheater. Italian authorities said they were working on determining the circumstances of the accident.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Hungary: EU Commission wants to unblock €4.2b in funding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c201d3aa4732a0d725fb59b3a58b4a5ba349334c6f60da0421047d4dbfe0fc19</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:43:41Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T10:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hungary-eu-commission-wants-to-unblock-_4-2b-in-funding/a-79386848--1c819fc4fb27.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-eu-commission-wants-to-unblock-€4-2b-in-funding/a-79386848?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Commission's president has argued that Budapest is strengthening the rule of law with Viktor Orban finally out of office. Funds had been blocked over corruption allegations under Hungary's former government.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>OECD says growth 'resilient' in 2026 despite Middle East war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6990f83bc108db4926054b717428338890d6b543fa2cae63e6335b6e11acabf7</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:43:41Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T09:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/oecd-says-growth-resilient-in-2026-despite-middle-east-war/a-79386625--7b0c955491ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/oecd-says-growth-resilient-in-2026-despite-middle-east-war/a-79386625?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The OECD group of industrialized nations put its 2026 growth forecast at 2.9%. It said investment in AI was helping drive growth, while the war in the Middle East was fueling inflation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Campus Project 2026: Georgia Takes Center Stage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79d89fb81422ea298864a84d8dfaf5e81dd1d61425bf851ab808854a50cc3f7f</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:43:41Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T09:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/campus-project-2026-georgia-takes-center-stage/a-79380639--efaea8063cd9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/campus-project-2026-georgia-takes-center-stage/a-79380639?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Beethovenfest exchange project brings German and Georgian musical traditions together. And the reasons go beyond music.</summary><category term="NRS-Import" /></entry><entry><title>El Nino explained: How the weather pattern affects hurricanes and tropical storms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:abeb4d52698c918b0e0eb19ec1da25ce3e0bafd9e265db64e36051ea3dd29011</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:43:41Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T09:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/el-nino-explained-how-the-weather-pattern-affects-hurricanes-and-tropical-storms/a-79382511--be7cc5c8c0e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/el-nino-explained-how-the-weather-pattern-affects-hurricanes-and-tropical-storms/a-79382511?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From drought to major floods and extreme heat, El Nino will have a huge impact on the world's weather. In the Atlantic, it could mean a season without hurricanes.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>UN General Assembly: Leaders discuss AI, global conflicts</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:690c4ee7aeac6543fda1e279a792f8fd5acaaaa9f6155b1d78fa581e511c2ab1</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:45:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T08:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/un-general-assembly-leaders-discuss-ai-global-conflicts/live-79366211--639a4d11c5ad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/un-general-assembly-leaders-discuss-ai-global-conflicts/live-79366211?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Day 2 of the UN General Assembly saw speeches from the leaders of Syria, Iran and Ukraine, among others. Additional topics that were expected to be discussed include climate change and AI. Follow DW live.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>China's new travel rules unsettle tech giants and talent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c540b6bb39a0864ac79e5ba1b09a2a33162db87a8456b198d599b4b7b9927c2c</id><updated>2026-09-23T19:43:41Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T08:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-new-travel-rules-unsettle-tech-giants-and-talent/a-79319937--16d904ca4025.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-new-travel-rules-unsettle-tech-giants-and-talent/a-79319937?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Beijing is locking the gates to stop expertise and capital in strategic industries from fleeing. The country accused of industrial-scale intellectual property theft now fears the West will take its own.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry></feed>
